OL,3,AMbappe sorry for 'ill-judged' Mao
OL,4,Aremark after backlash in China
OL,5,
OL,6,FKylian Mbappe has apologised for
OL,7,F"ill-judged" comments he made about
OL,8,Flate Chinese leader Mao Zedong which
OL,9,Fled to him being dropped by several
OL,10,FChinese brands.
OL,12,FMbappe had reportedly told French talk
OL,13,Fshow The Bridge the meme "that makes me
OL,14,Flaugh the most, it's the one where
OL,15,Fthere's a video of a guy, I think it's
OL,16,Fa Chinese dictator..." He then laughs
OL,17,Fas the clip cuts to a meme showing his
OL,18,Fface superimposed on an image
OL,19,Fresembling Mao.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
